-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 24A: POST-APPEAL APPLICATIONS IN CAPITAL CASES (rules 1 to 4), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc6-order-23.l4.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a condition introduced by "where", "unless" or "if", or a
--                time fixed in the text's own words and missed ("within 3 days", "at the same time as the filing",
--                "within the day on which"; ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must", or a grant
--                ("may") is limited by its own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every requirement here is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise (O 3 r 2(1)).
-- A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3 (roc1's range): each function takes the last day that Rule gives as the
-- input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.  "PACC" is not defined in these Rules: Rule 1(2) takes the meaning of the
-- expressions used in Division 4 of Part 5 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 from section 60F of that Act (outside the
-- sources).  The Order speaks of an application for PACC permission, and of a PACC application to be made where the Court of
-- Appeal grants that permission (Rule 3(1)).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 24A -- Post-appeal applications in capital cases`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- Interpretation and mode of application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3831 | 1. —(1) In this Order, “Act” means the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, and any reference to a section is, unless it is otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act. (2) Expressions used in this Order which are used in Division 4 of Part 5 of the Act have the meanings given by section 60F.
@ref O 24A r 1(1) (src:3831)
GIVEN `the enactment is the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 1(1) "Act" is the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969` MEANS
    IF `the enactment is the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Act” means the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969"

@ref O 24A r 1(1) (src:3831)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    IF `it is otherwise expressly provided`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless it is otherwise expressly provided", and what is provided is not stated here
    ELSE JUST `the reference is to a section in the Act` -- the reference is read as a reference to a section in the Act

-- src:3831 | 1. —(1) In this Order, “Act” means the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, and any reference to a section is, unless it is otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act. (2) Expressions used in this Order which are used in Division 4 of Part 5 of the Act have the meanings given by section 60F.
@ref O 24A r 1(2) (src:3831)
GIVEN `division 4 of part 5 of the act and section 60f give the expression this meaning` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 1(2) the expression has the meaning given by section 60F` MEANS
    `division 4 of part 5 of the act and section 60f give the expression this meaning` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when absent: section 60F of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 is not among the sources

DECLARE `o 24A r 1(3) the application` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A r 1(3)(a) an application for PACC permission`
    `o 24A r 1(3)(b) a PACC application`
    `o 24A r 1(3) some other application`

DECLARE `o 24A r 1(3) how the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A r 1(3) by originating application`
    `o 24A r 1(3) by summons in the originating application in which the application for PACC permission was granted`
    `o 24A r 1(3) in some other way`

-- src:3832 | (3) An application to which this Order applies must be made — ( a )
-- src:3833 | in the case of an application for PACC permission, by originating application; and
-- src:3834 | ( b )
-- src:3835 | in the case of a PACC application, by summons in the originating application in which the application for PACC permission was granted. [S 535/2024 wef 28/06/2024]
@ref O 24A r 1(3) (src:3832-3835)
GIVEN application IS A `o 24A r 1(3) the application`
      how IS A `o 24A r 1(3) how the application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 1(3) the application is made in the way required` MEANS
    CONSIDER application
    WHEN `o 24A r 1(3)(a) an application for PACC permission` THEN
        IF how EQUALS `o 24A r 1(3) by originating application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way
    WHEN `o 24A r 1(3)(b) a PACC application` THEN
        IF how EQUALS `o 24A r 1(3) by summons in the originating application in which the application for PACC permission was granted`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way
    WHEN `o 24A r 1(3) some other application` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application to which this Order applies"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- Application for PACC permission`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3837 | 2. —(1) For the purposes of section 60G(3), an application for PACC permission must be fixed for hearing within 21 days after the date on which the application is filed. (2) For the purposes of section 60G(4), the applicant in an application for PACC permission must file written submissions in support of the application, and the other documents mentioned in paragraph (4), at the same time as the filing of the application.
@ref O 24A r 2(1) (src:3837)
`o 24A r 2(1) twenty-one days` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 21
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- Fork F-O24A-1: "must be fixed for hearing within 21 days after the date on which the application is filed" can mean that
-- the hearing DATE falls within 21 days (taken here) or that the act of FIXING it is done within 21 days.
@ref O 24A r 2(1) (src:3837)
GIVEN `the hearing date fixed for the application` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(1) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within 21 days after it is filed` MEANS
    IF `the hearing date fixed for the application` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "within 21 days after the date on which the application is filed"

-- src:3837 | 2. —(1) For the purposes of section 60G(3), an application for PACC permission must be fixed for hearing within 21 days after the date on which the application is filed. (2) For the purposes of section 60G(4), the applicant in an application for PACC permission must file written submissions in support of the application, and the other documents mentioned in paragraph (4), at the same time as the filing of the application.
@ref O 24A r 2(2) (src:3837)
GIVEN `the date the application for PACC permission was filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the written submissions in support were filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the other documents mentioned in paragraph (4) were filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(2) the written submissions and the other documents are filed at the same time as the application` MEANS
    IF `the date the written submissions in support were filed` EQUALS `the date the application for PACC permission was filed` AND `the date the other documents mentioned in paragraph (4) were filed` EQUALS `the date the application for PACC permission was filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "at the same time as the filing of the application"

-- src:3838 | (3) The written submissions mentioned in paragraph (2) are subject to a page limit of 35 pages (including any cover page and contents page), unless the Court of Appeal otherwise allows.
@ref O 24A r 2(3) (src:3838)
`o 24A r 2(3) the page limit for the applicant's written submissions` MEANS 35

@ref O 24A r 2(3) (src:3838)
GIVEN `the number of pages, including any cover page and contents page` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court of Appeal otherwise allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(3) the written submissions are within the page limit` MEANS
    IF `the number of pages, including any cover page and contents page` AT MOST `o 24A r 2(3) the page limit for the applicant's written submissions` OR `the Court of Appeal otherwise allows`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to a page limit of 35 pages ..., unless the Court of Appeal otherwise allows"

-- The matters the counsel's affidavit states under paragraph (4)(a): (i) to (xi), with (vii) and (viii) each in two parts.
DECLARE `o 24A r 2(4)(a) matter stated by counsel` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(i) the date each counsel was instructed, and who instructed each`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(ii) the material that will be relied on in the PACC application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(iii) the date the material was first obtained`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(iv) why the material could not have been adduced before the relevant date with reasonable diligence`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(v) the reason for the interval between that date and the filing of the application for PACC permission`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vi) whether a similar argument was made before and whether it was dismissed`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vii)(A) the details of every application for review permission and every review application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vii)(B) the details of every other application for PACC permission and every PACC application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(viii)(A) the details of every other application made on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(viii)(B) the details of every action filed on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(ix) that each counsel genuinely believes the PACC application to be of merit`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(x) why each counsel believes the PACC application to be of merit and its legal arguments persuasive`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(xi) that each counsel is aware of the consequences of making a false statement in the affidavit`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(a) some other matter`

DECLARE `o 24A r 2(4)(b) matter stated by the applicant` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(i) the material that will be relied on in the PACC application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(ii) the date the applicant first obtained the material`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(iii) why the material could not have been adduced before the relevant date with reasonable diligence`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(iv) the reason for the interval between that date and the filing of the application for PACC permission`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(v)(A) the details of every application for review permission and every review application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(v)(B) the details of every other application for PACC permission and every PACC application`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(vi)(A) the details of every other application made on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(vi)(B) the details of every action filed on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b)(vii) whether the applicant is or was assisted by any person or organisation, and who and how`
    `o 24A r 2(4)(b) some other matter`

-- src:3839 | (4) For the purposes of section 60G(4), the other documents that the applicant in an application for PACC permission must file are as follows: ( a )
-- src:3840 | where the applicant is represented by one or more counsel, an affidavit made by the counsel (if only one counsel is appointed), or a separate affidavit made by each counsel as the deponent or a joint affidavit made by all of the counsel as deponents (if more than one counsel is appointed), stating all of the following: (i)
-- src:3841 | the date on which each counsel was instructed, and who instructed each counsel;
-- src:3842 | (ii)
-- src:3843 | the material (being evidence or legal arguments) that will be relied on in the PACC application to be made;
-- src:3844 | (iii)
-- src:3845 | the date on which the material mentioned in sub‑paragraph (ii) was first obtained, regardless whether by the applicant or the counsel;
-- src:3846 | (iv)
-- src:3847 | the reason why the material mentioned in sub‑paragraph (ii) could not have been adduced in Court before the relevant date, even with reasonable diligence;
-- src:3848 | (v)
-- src:3849 | the reason for the length of the interval of time between the date mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii) and the date on which the application for PACC permission is filed;
-- src:3850 | (vi)
-- src:3851 | whether any argument similar to that in the PACC application to be made had been made previously by any person in any Court and if so, whether the argument was dismissed by the Court;
-- src:3852 | (vii)
-- src:3853 | the details of — (A)
-- src:3854 | every application for review permission, and every review application, made by the applicant (whether alone or together with any other person) under Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010; and
-- src:3855 | (B)
-- src:3856 | every other application for PACC permission and every PACC application made by the applicant (whether alone or together with any other person),
-- src:3857 | with or without the involvement of any counsel (including the date and case number of such application, the order sought in such application, the decision of the Court in such application, and whether there was any finding of abuse of process in such application);
-- src:3858 | (viii)
-- src:3859 | the details of — (A)
-- src:3860 | every application (other than an application mentioned in sub‑paragraph (vii)) made by the applicant (whether alone or together with any other person) on or after 28 June 2024; and
-- src:3861 | (B)
-- src:3862 | every action filed by the applicant (whether alone or together with any other person) on or after 28 June 2024,
-- src:3863 | with or without the involvement of any counsel, in relation to which the Court of Appeal has found that the applicant had abused the process of the court in order to delay or frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death (including the date and case number of such application or action, the order sought in such application or action, and the decision of the Court in such application or action);
-- src:3864 | (ix)
-- src:3865 | that each counsel genuinely believes the PACC application to be made to be of merit;
-- src:3866 | (x)
-- src:3867 | the reason why each counsel believes the PACC application to be made to be of merit, including the reasons why the counsel believes the legal arguments in the PACC application to be made to be persuasive;
-- src:3868 | (xi)
-- src:3869 | that each counsel is aware of the consequences of making a false statement in the affidavit;
@ref O 24A r 2(4)(a) (src:3839-3869)
GIVEN `the applicant is represented by one or more counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters the affidavit made by counsel states` IS A LIST OF `o 24A r 2(4)(a) matter stated by counsel`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(4)(a) the counsel's affidavit states all the matters required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the applicant is represented by one or more counsel`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "where the applicant is represented by one or more counsel"
        IF all (GIVEN m YIELD elem m `the matters the affidavit made by counsel states`) `o 24A r 2(4)(a) all the matters` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the affidavit must state "all of the following" and does not say what follows if one is missing

`o 24A r 2(4)(a) all the matters` MEANS
    LIST
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(i) the date each counsel was instructed, and who instructed each`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(ii) the material that will be relied on in the PACC application`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(iii) the date the material was first obtained`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(iv) why the material could not have been adduced before the relevant date with reasonable diligence`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(v) the reason for the interval between that date and the filing of the application for PACC permission`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vi) whether a similar argument was made before and whether it was dismissed`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vii)(A) the details of every application for review permission and every review application`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(vii)(B) the details of every other application for PACC permission and every PACC application`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(viii)(A) the details of every other application made on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(viii)(B) the details of every action filed on or after 28 June 2024 found to be an abuse of process`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(ix) that each counsel genuinely believes the PACC application to be of merit`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(x) why each counsel believes the PACC application to be of merit and its legal arguments persuasive`,
        `o 24A r 2(4)(a)(xi) that each counsel is aware of the consequences of making a false statement in the affidavit`

