-- src:3898 | an applicant was not represented by any counsel when the application for PACC permission was filed, and appoints one or more counsel (by way of filing a notice of appointment of solicitor) to represent the applicant in the application for PACC permission after the filing of the application for PACC permission.
@ref O 24A r 2(7) (src:3895-3898)
GIVEN `the applicant was represented by one or more counsel when the application for PACC permission was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant appoints additional counsel or different counsel after the application was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant appoints one or more counsel after the application was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made by filing a notice of appointment of solicitor or notice of change of solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(7) paragraphs (8) and (9) apply to the applicant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the applicant was represented by one or more counsel when the application for PACC permission was filed` AND `the applicant appoints additional counsel or different counsel after the application was filed` AND `the appointment is made by filing a notice of appointment of solicitor or notice of change of solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF (NOT `the applicant was represented by one or more counsel when the application for PACC permission was filed`) AND `the applicant appoints one or more counsel after the application was filed` AND `the appointment is made by filing a notice of appointment of solicitor or notice of change of solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any of the following circumstances" names two

-- src:3899 | (8) For the purposes of section 60G(4), the applicant mentioned in paragraph (7) must, within 3 days after the appointment of the counsel mentioned in paragraph (7)( a ) or ( b ), file an affidavit made by the counsel (if only one counsel is appointed), or a separate affidavit made by each counsel as the deponent or a joint affidavit made by all of the counsel as deponents (if more than one counsel is appointed), that states all of the matters mentioned in paragraph (4)( a )(i) to (xi).
@ref O 24A r 2(8) (src:3899)
