`o 24A r 2(8) the affidavit of the newly appointed counsel is filed within 3 days after the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `paragraph (7) applies to the applicant`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the applicant mentioned in paragraph (7)"
        IF `the date the affidavit was filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "within 3 days after the appointment of the counsel"

@ref O 24A r 2(8) (src:3899)
GIVEN `the matters the affidavit states` IS A LIST OF `o 24A r 2(4)(a) matter stated by counsel`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 2(8) the affidavit states all the matters in paragraph (4)(a)(i) to (xi)` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN m YIELD elem m `the matters the affidavit states`) `o 24A r 2(4)(a) all the matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the affidavit "states all of the matters" and does not say what follows if one is missing

