-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- Appointment of solicitor in application for PACC permission or PACC application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3923 | 4. Where an applicant in an application for PACC permission or a PACC application who is represented by one or more counsel in that application decides to appoint one or more additional counsel (whether from the same firm as any counsel representing the applicant or from any other firm) for the purpose of that application, the applicant must file and serve a notice of appointment in Form 3 naming each additional counsel. [S 535/2024 wef 28/06/2024]
@ref O 24A r 4 (src:3923)
`o 24A r 4 the form of the notice of appointment` MEANS "Form 3"

@ref O 24A r 4 (src:3923)
GIVEN `the applicant is represented by one or more counsel in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant decides to appoint one or more additional counsel for the purpose of that application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 4 the applicant must file and serve a notice of appointment` MEANS
    IF `the applicant is represented by one or more counsel in the application` AND `the applicant decides to appoint one or more additional counsel for the purpose of that application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where an applicant ... who is represented by one or more counsel ... decides to appoint one or more additional counsel"

@ref O 24A r 4 (src:3923)
GIVEN `the form the notice is in` IS A STRING
      `the notice names each additional counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24A r 4 the notice of appointment is filed and served as required` MEANS
    IF `the form the notice is in` EQUALS `o 24A r 4 the form of the notice of appointment` AND `the notice names each additional counsel` AND `the notice was filed and served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says the applicant "must file and serve a notice of appointment in Form 3 naming each additional counsel" and does not say what follows if not

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The duties of Order 24A as regulative rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 24A party` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A the applicant`
    `o 24A the respondent`

DECLARE `o 24A act` IS ONE OF
    `o 24A r 3(1) make the PACC application to the Court of Appeal`
    `o 24A r 3(3)(b) file written submissions in support of the PACC application`
    `o 24A r 2(10) file written submissions in response`

-- src:3912 | 3. —(1) For the purposes of section 60H(1), where the Court of Appeal grants the application for PACC permission, the PACC application must be made to the Court of Appeal within 3 days after the date on which the permission is granted. (2) For the purposes of section 60H(1), a PACC application must be fixed for hearing within 21 days after the date on which the PACC application is made.
@ref O 24A r 3(1) (src:3912)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 24A party` `o 24A act`
`o 24A r 3(1) the applicant must make the PACC application within 3 days after permission is granted` MEANS
    PARTY `o 24A the applicant`
    MUST `o 24A r 3(1) make the PACC application to the Court of Appeal`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE
        PARTY `o 24A the applicant`
        MUST `o 24A r 3(3)(b) file written submissions in support of the PACC application`
        WITHIN 3
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the applicant did not file written submissions within 3 days after the PACC application was made"
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the applicant did not make the PACC application within 3 days after permission was granted"

-- src:3901 | (10) For the purposes of section 60G(5), the respondent in an application for PACC permission may file written submissions in relation to the application — ( a )
-- src:3902 | within 3 days after the date on which the application is filed and served on the respondent; and
@ref O 24A r 2(10)(a) (src:3901-3902)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 24A party` `o 24A act`
`o 24A r 2(10) the respondent may file written submissions within 3 days after the application is filed and served` MEANS
    PARTY `o 24A the respondent`
    MAY `o 24A r 2(10) file written submissions in response`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
